   "dir": "/Volumes/T7/guided-analysis/tools/bench-runs/2026-10-09/claude_claude-haiku-5-5/jahncke2025-dag1-mipsc/run1/home/sessions/20261009-050212-27d1",
   "answer": "## mIPSC results: Ctrl versus cKO (Dag1 conditional knockout)\n\n**Caution:** the reader found 1 sweep in all 32 files. You described 10 sweeps. This conflict is not resolved. The results below use one sweep per cell.\n\n### Settings used (decision record)\n- Event detection method: template (Clements and Bekkers).\n- Event direction: inward.\n- Template rise: 0.7 ms. Template decay: 8 ms.\n- Event threshold: 4 times the noise SD. The decision record sets this value. You own it. I did not find your answer to this value in my log.\n- Filter: none.\n- Analysis window: 1 to 29.5 s.\n- Sweeps: all.\n- Liquid junction potential: not corrected.\n- Unit of replication for the main test: cells.\n- Test: Welch t-test. Alpha: 0.05.\n\n### What I did\n1. Read the cell list and the metadata file. The metadata file is malformed. Each cell name sits on one line. Its animal and group sit on the next line. I wrote a corrected copy, cells_metadata_clean.csv. The original file is unchanged. You did not confirm the corrected copy.\n2. Checked the sweep count in all 32 cell files with the inspection tool. Each file has 1 sweep of 29.9999 s at 10000 Hz.\n3. Detected mIPSCs in all 32 cells with the settings above. Each cell analyzed 28.5 s.\n4. Joined the cell results to the corrected metadata. Ran a Welch t-test with each cell as one observation (cKO minus Ctrl).\n\n### Groups (step 1)\n- Ctrl: 16 cells from 6 animals.\n- cKO: 16 cells from 6 animals.\n\n### Frequency and amplitude (step 2, chosen settings)\n- Mean frequency: Ctrl 2.62 Hz; cKO 1.64 Hz.\n- Mean amplitude: Ctrl 55.6 pA; cKO 40.2 pA.\n\n### Group comparison (step 3, cells as observations, Welch t-test)\n- Frequency: cKO minus Ctrl −0.98 Hz (95% CI −1.83 to −0.14). p = 0.024. Adjusted p (Benjamini-Hochberg, four features) = 0.048. Cohen d = −0.84. Significant at alpha 0.05 after adjustment.\n- Amplitude: cKO minus Ctrl −15.4 pA (95% CI −27.2 to −3.6). p = 0.012. Adjusted p = 0.048. Cohen d = −0.94. Significant at alpha 0.05 after adjustment.\n\n### Kinetics (step 4, cells as observations, Welch t-test)\n- Mean decay time constant, Ctrl: 8.14 ms.\n- 10–90% rise time: Ctrl 0.92 ms; cKO 1.00 ms. p = 0.269 (adjusted p 0.269). Not significant.\n- Decay time constant: Ctrl 8.14 ms; cKO 7.32 ms. p = 0.178 (adjusted p 0.237). Not significant.\n\n### Checks (comparison runs, not the chosen settings)\n- **Animal as the unit (comparison run):** no feature passes the adjusted p value at alpha 0.05. The smallest raw p is 0.027. The smallest adjusted p is 0.062.\n- **Threshold (comparison run):** mean amplitude over all 32 cells is 37.8 pA at 3 times the noise SD and 57.2 pA at 5 times. The chosen threshold of 4 times gives 47.9 pA. I did not obtain a frequency at thresholds 3 or 5. My two direct runs at those values returned the recorded threshold of 4, so they do not count as results.\n- **Non-independence:** cells in one animal share variance. The intraclass correlation for the animal is up to 0.30. So the cell-level p values above are likely too small. A mixed model with the animal as a random effect is the correct test here: lme4 lmer(feature ~ group + (1 | animal)). I did not run this model.\n\n### What is uncertain\n- **Sweep count.** The reader finds 1 sweep in all 32 files. You described 10 sweeps. I did not check the files in Igor Pro. If 10 sweeps exist, the counts, frequencies and means change.\n- **Threshold.** Frequency and amplitude depend on the threshold. The frequency at other thresholds is not known from this session.\n- **Metadata.** The corrected copy is my reading of the file. You did not confirm it.\n- **Group evidence.** The cell-level p values may overstate the evidence. The animal-level check does not show a significant group difference.\n\n### What waits for you\n1. Confirm the event threshold (the record value is 4 times the noise SD).\n2. Check the sweep count in Igor Pro. If 10 sweeps exist, I run all analyses again.\n3. Confirm the corrected metadata copy, cells_metadata_clean.csv.\n4. Decide whether the main result uses the cell-level test or the mixed model with the animal as a random effect.\n\nFiles: cell_features_mipsc.csv (one row per cell), group_comparison.csv, events.png and group_comparison.png in the session folder.\n\nStep results that the answer does not mention, from the record:\n- n2 run_script: The script ran in /Volumes/T7/guided-analysis/tools/bench-runs/2026-10-09/claude_claude-haiku-5-5/jahncke2025-dag1-mipsc/run1/home/sessions/20261009-050212-27d1/work and wrote 0 new file(s) to /Volumes/T7/guided-analysis/tools/bench-runs/2026-10-09/claude_claude-haiku-5-5/jahncke2025-dag1-mipsc/run1/home/sessions/20261009-050212-27d1/work.\n- n11 run_script: The script ran in /Volumes/T7/guided-analysis/tools/bench-runs/2026-10-09/claude_claude-haiku-5-5/jahncke2025-dag1-mipsc/run1/home/sessions/20261009-050212-27d1/work and wrote 2 new file(s) to /Volumes/T7/guided-analysis/tools/bench-runs/2026-10-09/claude_claude-haiku-5-5/jahncke2025-dag1-mipsc/run1/home/sessions/20261009-050212-27d1/work.\n- n48 run_script: The script ran in /Volumes/T7/guided-analysis/tools/bench-runs/2026-10-09/claude_claude-haiku-5-5/jahncke2025-dag1-mipsc/run1/home/sessions/20261009-050212-27d1/work and wrote 96 new file(s) to /Volumes/T7/guided-analysis/tools/bench-runs/2026-10-09/claude_claude-haiku-5-5/jahncke2025-dag1-mipsc/run1/home/sessions/20261009-050212-27d1/work.\n\nSettings used, from the decision record: Sweeps to include: all · Event detection method: template · Event detection threshold (times the noise SD): 4 · Direction of the events: inward · Expected event rise time constant (ms): 0.7 · Expected event decay time constant (ms): 8 · Unit of replication for the group comparison: cells · Test for the difference between two groups: t · Significance level (alpha): 0.05.",
